{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggybgspsSv2mAi251TMR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VpAeJh545ytVfy3UbMoqR7","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/micha/.cache/plan-x8534bd-wzXO/hub/ai-hub/lib/hub; cat $H/retrofit.md; echo; echo \"======== session.js head\"; sed -n 1,80p $H/session.js","description":"Read hub retrofit notes and session client header"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7592,"cache_read_input_tokens":121637,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7592},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ff8a465-a3dc-4463-ad61-3d7e016e47ef","uuid":"a10c58c7-061a-467f-93eb-03faecfd5c54","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:55:30.027Z","request_id":"req_011CggybgegRVKQB4maYR5Ub","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VpAeJh545ytVfy3UbMoqR7":{"command":"H=/home/micha/.cache/plan-x8534bd-wzXO/hub/ai-hub/lib/hub; cat $H/retrofit.md; echo; echo \"======== session.js head\"; sed -n 1,80p $H/session.js","description":"Read hub retrofit notes and session client header"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VpAeJh545ytVfy3UbMoqR7","type":"tool_result","content":"# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n\n---\n\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\n\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\nagainst it:\n\n<protocol>\n{{contract}}\n</protocol>\n\nDo only this:\n\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\n   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press\n   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\n   `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })` once. In\n   `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current score at once if the run is\n   still going.\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\n\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\nlike). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the\ngame an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for\neither. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol\ndescribes; you need not run them, the hub does.\n\nIf the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one\nline: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.\n\nOtherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line\nyou changed.\n\n{{notes}}\n\n======== session.js head\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\n      },\n    };\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\n    return new Proxy(api, {\n      get: function (t, k) {\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\n      },\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\n        return true;\n      },\n      has: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data || k in t;\n      },\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\n        delete data[k];\n        return true;","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ff8a465-a3dc-4463-ad61-3d7e016e47ef","uuid":"90ea8a97-d68e-4902-b21a-cbbcc9fc07d1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:55:30.271Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Upgrading an existing game to parallel\n\nThe prompt `scripts/retrofit.mjs` gives a model for each game, after its tool\nstep has put the session client and the parallel metas at the top of the\npage. The model works in a copy of the game in a folder of its own: `{{file}}`\nis the game's page there, `{{contract}}` the protocol in\n[`README.md`](README.md) from *Modes* to *Rules*, word for word (the same text\nfor every game, so a batch reads it from the cache), `{{budget}}` the most lines a try may change,\nand `{{notes}}` what the last try's check said, if there was one.\n\n---\n\nYou are upgrading one existing browser game, `{{file}}`, so friends can play it\nin parallel mode in AI Hub sessions: each friend plays their own copy at the same\ntime, and the hub keeps the score. Change as little as possible. Never change\nhow the game plays or feels: movement, physics, timing, controls, menus, art,\naudio and difficulty stay exactly as they are.\n\nA tool has already put the session client (`session.js`, which defines\n`window.AIHub`) and the `hub:session` meta tags at the top of `<head>`. This is\nthe protocol; the game is upgraded to its parallel mode, and the hub checks it\nagainst it:\n\n<protocol>\n{{contract}}\n</protocol>\n\nDo only this:\n\n1. Find how the game is won or scored. Use a time (lower wins) if it has a\n   clear finish, otherwise its score (higher wins).\n2. Fill `hub:session-goal` (how to win, at most 60 characters) and\n   `hub:session-howto` (the controls, at most 80 characters), in plain words\n   for someone who has never seen the game. If a round of the game has a\n   fixed length, add `<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"…\">` with it.\n   If the game cannot run at all without WebGPU, also add\n   `<meta name=\"hub:webgpu\" content=\"required\">`.\n3. In session mode (`AIHub.active` is true): skip the title screen, attract\n   mode and menus; `await AIHub.connect({ mode: 'parallel', seats: [1, 4] })`;\n   build the game; call `AIHub.ready()` as soon as it can start, with no \"press\n   start\" prompt; begin play only once `AIHub.time() >= 0`. If `connect()`\n   answers `null`, carry on as when `AIHub.active` is false.\n4. Whenever the score changes, call\n   `AIHub.progress({ score: <number>, label: <short text> })`, where a higher\n   score is further ahead and `label` is short text for the scoreboard.\n5. When the run ends (finished, died, out of lives), call\n   `AIHub.result({ time })` or `AIHub.result({ score })` once. In\n   `AIHub.on('time-up', …)`, report the current score at once if the run is\n   still going.\n6. In `AIHub.on('end', …)`, stop input and sound.\n7. If the game deals its pieces, cards, board or level layout from one\n   function using `Math.random`, make that function draw from\n   `AIHub.rng('deal')` in session mode, so every copy gets the same deal all\n   round. Leave every other random call alone.\n8. When `AIHub.active` is false, the game must behave exactly as before.\n\nDon't add features, refactor, reformat, rename or upgrade anything, and don't\ntouch code these steps don't need: change at most {{budget}} lines. Never edit\nthe session client between its `/*! aihub-session` banner and its last line,\nthe names of the meta tags, or a bundled library (three.js, Rapier and the\nlike). Saved progress is already hidden in a session (the client gives the\ngame an empty storage), and `Math.random` is already seeded: add no code for\neither. You are done when the game would pass the checks the protocol\ndescribes; you need not run them, the hub does.\n\nIf the game has no score and no finish, change nothing and reply with one\nline: `NOT PARALLEL: <why>`.\n\nOtherwise reply with: the score or time used, the end condition, and every line\nyou changed.\n\n{{notes}}\n\n======== session.js head\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\n      },\n    };\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\n    return new Proxy(api, {\n      get: function (t, k) {\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\n      },\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\n        return true;\n      },\n      has: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data || k in t;\n      },\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\n        delete data[k];\n        return true;","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01VpAeJh545ytVfy3UbMoqR7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cggyckn1cady4wfSZy4S5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01B5L1PncXAmiRoj6roPxchG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"H=/home/micha/.cache/plan-x8534bd-wzXO/hub/ai-hub/lib/hub; ls -la $H/examples; echo \"====== arena.html\"; cat $H/examples/arena.html | head -400","description":"Read the hub's shared-world arena example"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3542,"cache_read_input_tokens":129229,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3542},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ff8a465-a3dc-4463-ad61-3d7e016e47ef","uuid":"9b4c8f2e-3121-459c-8a16-9554bf438a44","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:55:33.302Z","request_id":"req_011CggyckWP13DhtDjYYbyrH","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01B5L1PncXAmiRoj6roPxchG":{"command":"H=/home/micha/.cache/plan-x8534bd-wzXO/hub/ai-hub/lib/hub; ls -la $H/examples; echo \"====== arena.html\"; cat $H/examples/arena.html | head -400","description":"Read the hub's shared-world arena example"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01B5L1PncXAmiRoj6roPxchG","type":"tool_result","content":"total 112\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 17:53 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 17:53 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 33330 Nov  3 17:53 arena.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 29231 Nov  3 17:53 ghost.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 33011 Nov  3 17:53 parallel.html\n====== arena.html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Star Arena — AI Hub session example (shared world)</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"A minimal shared-world game for the AI Hub Session Protocol: every copy moves its own player, the host runs the stars and the scores, first to ten wins.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1b1530\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Tech demo\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"2\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"First to ten stars wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: arrows, WASD or a stick · sprint: Space or Cross · or hold a finger\">\n<style>\n  html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #1b1530; color: #f3eef7; font: 16px system-ui, sans-serif; overflow: hidden; }\n  canvas { display: block; width: 100%; height: 100%; touch-action: none; }\n</style>\n<script>\n/*! aihub-session 1.4.0 — AI Hub Session Protocol v1 client. Paste it into your game unmodified. */\n(function (root) {\n  'use strict';\n  if (root.AIHub) return;\n\n  var VERSION = '1.4.0';\n  var HELLO_EVERY_MS = 500;\n  var HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS = 10000;\n  var PROGRESS_EVERY_MS = 1000;\n  /** The hub's welcome may change these; a newer hub never needs a newer copy of this file for it. */\n  var limits = { maxBytes: 16384, ratePerS: 20, burst: 40 };\n\n  var framed = false;\n  try {\n    framed = root.parent && root.parent !== root;\n  } catch (e) {\n    framed = true;\n  }\n  var search = String(root.location && root.location.search);\n  var flagged = /[?&]aihub=/.test(search);\n  var seedArg = /[?&]aihub-seed=(\\d+)/.exec(search);\n\n  var hub = {\n    version: VERSION,\n    protocol: 1,\n    /** True when the hub launched this page for a session (?aihub=1 inside a frame). */\n    active: !!(flagged && framed),\n    me: null,\n    host: null,\n    isHost: false,\n    players: [],\n    mode: null,\n    seed: 0,\n    limitMs: 0,\n    round: 0,\n    /** True when the hub shows the round's splash and collects every player's ready: call ready() once loaded, with no prompt. */\n    splash: false,\n    /** True when the hub seeded Math.random for this round (side by side): every copy draws the same numbers. */\n    seeded: false,\n  };\n\n  /** A storage that lives and dies with the page: the Storage methods, and items as properties too. */\n  function memoryStorage() {\n    var data = Object.create(null);\n    var api = {\n      getItem: function (k) {\n        k = String(k);\n        return k in data ? data[k] : null;\n      },\n      setItem: function (k, v) {\n        data[String(k)] = String(v);\n      },\n      removeItem: function (k) {\n        delete data[String(k)];\n      },\n      clear: function () {\n        for (var k in data) delete data[k];\n      },\n      key: function (i) {\n        var keys = Object.keys(data);\n        return i >= 0 && i < keys.length ? keys[i] : null;\n      },\n    };\n    if (typeof Proxy !== 'function') return api;\n    return new Proxy(api, {\n      get: function (t, k) {\n        if (k === 'length') return Object.keys(data).length;\n        if (typeof k === 'symbol' || k in t) return t[k];\n        return k in data ? data[k] : undefined;\n      },\n      set: function (t, k, v) {\n        if (typeof k !== 'symbol') data[k] = String(v);\n        return true;\n      },\n      has: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data || k in t;\n      },\n      deleteProperty: function (t, k) {\n        delete data[k];\n        return true;\n      },\n      ownKeys: function () {\n        return Object.keys(data);\n      },\n      getOwnPropertyDescriptor: function (t, k) {\n        return k in data ? { value: data[k], writable: true, enumerable: true, configurable: true } : undefined;\n      },\n    });\n  }\n\n  /** mulberry32: numbers in [0, 1), the same sequence everywhere for the same 32-bit start. */\n  function generator(a) {\n    return function () {\n      a = (a + 0x6d2b79f5) >>> 0;\n      var t = a;\n      t = Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 15), t | 1);\n      t ^= t + Math.imul(t ^ (t >>> 7), t | 61);\n      return ((t ^ (t >>> 14)) >>> 0) / 4294967296;\n    };\n  }\n\n  // A fair start: in a session the game gets an empty storage of its own, so\n  // every round starts as a first launch (no saved unlocks, upgrades or runs),\n  // and nothing the round saves touches the player's own saves.\n  if (hub.active) {\n    for (var s = 0, stores = ['localStorage', 'sessionStorage']; s < stores.length; s++) {\n      try {\n        Object.defineProperty(root, stores[s], { configurable: true, value: memoryStorage() });\n      } catch (e) {\n        warn('could not give the game a fresh ' + stores[s]);\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  // Side by side: before any of the game's own scripts run, Math.random becomes\n  // a generator seeded by the hub, so every copy builds the same start.\n  var realRandom = Math.random;\n  var seededRandom = null;\n  if (hub.active && seedArg) {\n    Math.random = seededRandom = generator(Number(seedArg[1]) >>> 0);\n    hub.seeded = true;\n  }\n\n  // In a session the hub owns fullscreen: a game that asks for it gets the\n  // hub's whole page, so the scoreboard and the hub's cards stay on top. The\n  // hub says when its page goes in and out, so the game's own toggle and its\n  // fullscreenchange listeners work as they always did.\n  var fullscreenOn = false;\n  if (hub.active && root.Element && root.document) {\n    var asks = function (on) {\n      return function () {\n        post('fullscreen', { on: on });\n        return Promise.resolve();\n      };\n    };\n    var proto = root.Element.prototype;\n    proto.requestFullscreen = proto.webkitRequestFullscreen = asks(true);\n    root.document.exitFullscreen = root.document.webkitExitFullscreen = asks(false);\n    var shown = function () {\n      return fullscreenOn ? root.document.documentElement || null : null;\n    };\n    try {\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'fullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n      Object.defineProperty(root.document, 'webkitFullscreenElement', { configurable: true, get: shown });\n    } catch (e) {}\n  }\n\n  /**\n   * No hub after all: play on, with Math.random the page's own again. The\n   * empty storage stays: the game has read it already, and what it writes\n   * must never land on the player's real saves.\n   */\n  function standAlone() {\n    hub.active = false;\n    if (seededRandom && Math.random === seededRandom) Math.random = realRandom;\n    hub.seeded = false;\n  }\n\n  var origin = '*';\n  var welcomed = false;\n  var ended = false;\n  var connecting = null;\n  var goAt = null;\n  var sentReady = false;\n  var reported = false;\n  var handlers = {};\n  var pending = {};\n  var tokens = limits.burst;\n  var refilled = now();\n  var probeFn = null;\n  var lastProgress = -Infinity;\n  var nextProgress = null;\n  var progressTimer = null;\n\n  function now() {\n    return root.performance && root.performance.now ? root.performance.now() : Date.now();\n  }\n\n  function warn(text) {\n    if (root.console) root.console.warn('[AIHub] ' + text);\n  }\n\n  function own(o, k) {\n    return Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(o, k);\n  }\n\n  /** This client's own fields, which no welcome may overwrite. */\n  var KEEP = { aihub: 1, type: 1, version: 1, protocol: 1, active: 1, seeded: 1 };\n\n  /** A plain JSON copy, or undefined when it is not JSON. */\n  function json(value) {\n    try {\n      var text = JSON.stringify(value);\n      return text === undefined ? undefined : JSON.parse(text);\n    } catch (e) {\n      return undefined;\n    }\n  }\n\n  function post(type, fields) {\n    var msg = { aihub: 1, type: type };\n    for (var key in fields) if (own(fields, key)) msg[key] = fields[key];\n    try {\n      root.parent.postMessage(msg, origin);\n    } catch (e) {\n      warn('could not reach the hub: ' + e.message);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function emit(type, args) {\n    var list = handlers[type];\n    if (!list || !list.length || pending[type]) {\n      (pending[type] = pending[type] || []).push(args);\n      return;\n    }\n    for (var i = 0; i < list.length; i++) {\n      try {\n        list[i].apply(null, args);\n      } catch (e) {\n        setTimeout(function () {\n          throw e;\n        });\n      }\n    }\n  }\n\n  function onMessage(event) {\n    if (event.source !== root.parent) return;\n    var m = event.data;\n    if (!m || m.aihub !== 1 || typeof m.type !== 'string') return;\n    if (m.type === 'welcome') {\n      if (welcomed) return;\n      welcomed = true;\n      origin = event.origin && event.origin !== 'null' ? event.origin : '*';\n      // Every field the hub sends is kept, so a newer hub can add one without a newer client.\n      for (var key in m) {\n        if (!own(m, key) || KEEP[key] || typeof hub[key] === 'function') continue;\n        hub[key] = m[key];\n      }\n      hub.players = (m.players || []).slice();\n      hub.seed = m.seed >>> 0;\n      hub.isHost = m.me === m.host;\n      hub.splash = m.splash === true;\n      if (m.limits) {\n        for (var l in limits) if (own(limits, l) && Number(m.limits[l]) > 0) limits[l] = Number(m.limits[l]);\n        tokens = limits.burst;\n      }\n      if (connecting) connecting.resolve(info());\n      return;\n    }\n    if (m.type === 'fullscreen') {\n      fullscreenOn = m.on === true;\n      try {\n        root.document.dispatchEvent(new root.Event('fullscreenchange'));\n      } catch (e) {}\n      return;\n    }\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return;\n    if (m.type === 'start') {\n      goAt = now() + Number(m.in || 0);\n      emit('start', [{ in: Number(m.in || 0) }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'message') {\n      emit('message', [m.data, m.from]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'leave') {\n      hub.players = hub.players.filter(function (p) {\n        return p.id !== m.id;\n      });\n      emit('leave', [{ id: m.id, reason: m.reason }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'time-up') {\n      emit('time-up', [{ graceMs: m.graceMs }]);\n    } else if (m.type === 'end') {\n      ended = true;\n      if (progressTimer) clearTimeout(progressTimer);\n      emit('end', [{ reason: m.reason, standings: m.standings || null }]);\n    } else {\n      // An event this client has never heard of: hand it on as it came.\n      var detail = {};\n      for (var k in m) if (own(m, k) && k !== 'aihub' && k !== 'type') detail[k] = m[k];\n      emit(m.type, [detail]);\n    }\n  }\n\n  function info() {\n    var out = {};\n    for (var key in hub) if (own(hub, key) && typeof hub[key] !== 'function' && !KEEP[key]) out[key] = hub[key];\n    out.players = hub.players.slice();\n    return out;\n  }\n\n  /** Join the session. Resolves with the round's info, or null when there is no hub: play normally. */\n  hub.connect = function (opts) {\n    if (connecting) return connecting.promise;\n    var done;\n    var promise = new Promise(function (resolve) {\n      done = resolve;\n    });\n    connecting = { promise: promise, resolve: done };\n    if (!hub.active) {\n      done(null);\n      return promise;\n    }\n    opts = opts || {};\n    root.addEventListener('message', onMessage);\n    var started = now();\n    var hello = function () {\n      if (welcomed) return;\n      if (now() - started > HELLO_TIMEOUT_MS) {\n        standAlone();\n        warn('no hub answered; playing normally');\n        done(null);\n        return;\n      }\n      post('hello', { v: 1, client: VERSION, mode: opts.mode || null, seats: opts.seats || null, card: opts.card === true });\n      setTimeout(hello, HELLO_EVERY_MS);\n    };\n    hello();\n    return promise;\n  };\n\n  /** Everything is loaded: at once when info.splash, otherwise from the player's ready gesture. */\n  hub.ready = function () {\n    if (!welcomed || sentReady || ended) return;\n    sentReady = true;\n    post('ready', {});\n  };\n\n  /** On the game's own card (connect({ card: true })): this player is 'ready', or asks for 'more' time (again takes it back). */\n  hub.answer = function (what) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended || goAt !== null) return;\n    if (what !== 'ready' && what !== 'more') return warn('answer is ready or more');\n    post('answer', { answer: what });\n  };\n\n  hub.on = function (type, fn) {\n    (handlers[type] = handlers[type] || []).push(fn);\n    if (pending[type] && !pending[type].flushing) {\n      pending[type].flushing = true;\n      setTimeout(function () {\n        var queued = pending[type];\n        delete pending[type];\n        for (var i = 0; i < queued.length; i++) emit(type, queued[i]);\n      });\n    }\n    return function () {\n      var list = handlers[type] || [];\n      var at = list.indexOf(fn);\n      if (at !== -1) list.splice(at, 1);\n    };\n  };\n\n  /** Send JSON data to every other player, or to one with {to: id}. {reliable: false} may drop or reorder. */\n  hub.send = function (data, opts) {\n    if (!welcomed || ended) return false;\n    opts = opts || {};\n    var text;\n    try {\n      text = JSON.stringify(data);\n    } catch (e) {\n      warn('send: data is not JSON');\n      return false;\n    }\n    if (text === undefined) return false;\n    if (text.length > limits.maxBytes) {\n      warn('send: message over ' + limits.maxBytes + ' bytes dropped');\n      return false;\n    }\n    var t = now();\n    tokens = Math.min(limits.burst, tokens + ((t - refilled) / 1000) * limits.ratePerS);\n    refilled = t;\n    if (tokens < 1) {\n      warn('send: over ' + limits.ratePerS + ' messages a second, dropped');\n      return false;\n    }\n    tokens -= 1;\n    var fields = { data: JSON.parse(text), reliable: opts.reliable !== false };\n    if (opts.to !== undefined && opts.to !== null) fields.to = opts.to;\n    post('send', fields);\n    return true;\n  };","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ff8a465-a3dc-4463-ad61-3d7e016e47ef","uuid":"daf47dc4-d838-409a-a871-0ce4949369e2","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:55:33.651Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"total 112\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 17:53 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 3 micha micha  4096 Nov  3 17:53 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 33330 Nov  3 17:53 arena.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 29231 Nov  3 17:53 ghost.html\n-rw-r--r-- 1 micha micha 33011 Nov  3 17:53 parallel.html\n====== arena.html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\">\n<title>Star Arena — AI Hub session example (shared world)</title>\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"A minimal shared-world game for the AI Hub Session Protocol: every copy moves its own player, the host runs the stars and the scores, first to ten wins.\">\n<meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#1b1530\">\n<meta name=\"hub:type\" content=\"Tech demo\">\n<meta name=\"hub:players\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session\" content=\"1\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-players\" content=\"2-4\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-mode\" content=\"shared-world\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-minutes\" content=\"2\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-goal\" content=\"First to ten stars wins\">\n<meta name=\"hub:session-howto\" content=\"Move: arrows, WASD or a stick · sprint: Space or Cross · or hold a finger\">\n<style>\n  html, body { margin: 0; heigh