ldLines\":3,\"newStart\":439,\"newLines\":4,\"lines\":[\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"model\\\":\\\"claude-opus-5-5\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"msg_011CggynuPCUUama2nXNbQNv\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\",\\\"role\\\":\\\"assistant\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_use\\\",\\\"id\\\":\\\"toolu_01SSoY1sNjp6aYyqoPgFK9RH\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /home/micha/.cache/crackmania-plan-research-xbd1c73/engine/dist/handoff && grep -n \\\\\\\"^- \\\\\\\\`audio\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\|^- \\\\\\\\`game.audio\\\\\\\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-260 | head -50\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"List the audio API entries in the index\\\"},\\\"caller\\\":{\\\"type\\\":\\\"direct\\\"}}],\\\"container\\\":null,\\\"stop_reason\\\":null,\\\"stop_sequence\\\":null,\\\"stop_details\\\":null,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":2,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":10244,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":201773,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":10244},\\\"output_tokens\\\":6,\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"global\\\",\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"input_transformations\\\":[],\\\"diagnostics\\\":null,\\\"context_management\\\":null},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"0d6fb019-3db7-4cee-b317-1fd1dbcfb5fc\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-04T00:57:57.826Z\\\",\\\"request_id\\\":\\\"req_011Cggynu85LUanTpjoKumd8\\\",\\\"wire_tool_inputs\\\":{\\\"toolu_01SSoY1sNjp6aYyqoPgFK9RH\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"cd /home/micha/.cache/crackmania-plan-research-xbd1c73/engine/dist/handoff && grep -n \\\\\\\"^- \\\\\\\\`audio\\\\\\\\.\\\\\\\\|^- \\\\\\\\`game.audio\\\\\\\" API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-260 | head -50\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"List the audio API entries in the index\\\"}}}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"message\\\":{\\\"role\\\":\\\"user\\\",\\\"content\\\":[{\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01SSoY1sNjp6aYyqoPgFK9RH\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"tool_result\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"514:- `game.audio`: chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song)\\\\n1051:- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\\\\n1052:- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\\\\n1053:- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to s\\\\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\\\\n1055:- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\\\\n1056:- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\\\\n1057:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .'\\\\n1058:- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\\\\n1059:- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\\\\n1060:- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's volume), \\\\n1061:- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\\\\n1062:- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\\\\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music pl\\\\n1064:- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\\\\n1065:- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\\\\n1066:- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\\\\n1067:- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\\\\n1068:- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\\\\n1069:- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\\\\n1070:- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\\\\n1071:- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\\\\n1072:- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\\\\n1073:- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\\\\n1074:- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\\\\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\\\\n1076:- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\\\\n1077:- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\\\\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work\\\",\\\"is_error\\\":false}]},\\\"parent_tool_use_id\\\":null,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"ca9ad09a-883e-41a0-9ad9-6fa5bd845840\\\",\\\"timestamp\\\":\\\"2026-11-04T00:57:57.852Z\\\",\\\"tool_use_result\\\":{\\\"stdout\\\":\\\"514:- `game.audio`: chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song)\\\\n1051:- `game.audio.applyVolume()`: apply volume, musicVolume, sfxVolume and mute after setting them directly (setVolume and mute call it)\\\\n1052:- `game.audio.at(step, fn)` †: call fn(step) on the update step the music reaches step (counted from its start, on as it loops); the song's change cancels it. Returns { cancel() }\\\\n1053:- `game.audio.calibrate()` †: the audio offset's calibration: a click on each beat (100 bpm, the first of a bar higher) as the music; tap(time) on each one heard (an event's timeStamp, or nothing: this update step). After 8 taps, result is the offset to s\\\\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\\\\n1055:- `game.audio.duck(on = true)`: quiet the music (to 35%) while on: under a game's own pause, map or dialog screen. The engine also ducks it while game.paused\\\\n1056:- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\\\\n1057:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .'\\\\n1058:- `game.audio.mute(on = !this.muted)`: toggle (or set) mute; returns the new state\\\\n1059:- `game.audio.onBeat(fn)` †: call fn(beat, pos) on the update step of each beat of whatever music plays (a dancer's step, a light's pulse). Returns { cancel() }\\\\n1060:- `game.audio.pos` †: where the music is, on the game's clock (headless too): { t: seconds since it started, step (from 0, counting on as it loops), beat, bar (four beats), at (the step in its loop), loop (times round), bpm, layers (each track's volume), \\\\n1061:- `game.audio.ready`: true once the browser lets the game make sound\\\\n1062:- `game.audio.setVolume(v)`: set the master volume, 0..1\\\\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music pl\\\\n1064:- `game.audio.sting(song, o = {})` †: play a short song once over the music (a goal's jingle): o.at 'now', 'beat' or 'bar' (on the music's next beat or bar), o.duck (the music's volume under it, .4)\\\\n1065:- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\\\\n1066:- `game.audio.tempo(bpm)` †: change the music's tempo as it plays (hurry up!): where it is stays, the steps after come at the new bpm\\\\n1067:- `game.audio.anchors = 0` †: how many times the sound was moved to meet the clock\\\\n1068:- `game.audio.ctx = null`: the Web Audio context, made at the first sound (null before, or where there is none)\\\\n1069:- `game.audio.drift = 0` †: what is heard against the game's clock at the last frame (seconds: the sound follows the clock, so it stays near 0)\\\\n1070:- `game.audio.ducked = false`: true while duck(true) holds the music down\\\\n1071:- `game.audio.failed = null`: why there is no sound (a message), or null\\\\n1072:- `game.audio.musicVolume = .5`, `game.audio.sfxVolume = 1`: 0..1 for effects and music\\\\n1073:- `game.audio.muted = false`: true while mute() is on\\\\n1074:- `game.audio.offset = 0` †: seconds the music sounds early, for speakers and headphones that lag (settings.audioOffset)\\\\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\\\\n1076:- `game.audio.song = null`: the music playing (null for none)\\\\n1077:- `game.audio.volume = .7`: master volume 0..1\\\",\\\"stderr\\\":\\\"\\\\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/work\\\",\\\"interrupted\\\":false,\\\"isImage\\\":false,\\\"noOutputExpected\\\":false},\\\"tool_result_meta\\\":[{\\\"id\\\":\\\"toolu_01SSoY1sNjp6aYyqoPgFK9RH\\\",\\\"permission_decision\\\":{\\\"decision\\\":\\\"accept\\\",\\\"source\\\":\\\"config\\\",\\\"reason_type\\\":\\\"mode\\\"}}]}\",\" {\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":50,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":50,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"e6856ad7-91c1-42d2-b894-1649e636372e\\\"}\",\"+{\\\"type\\\":\\\"system\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"thinking_tokens\\\",\\\"estimated_tokens\\\":150,\\\"estimated_tokens_delta\\\":100,\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"1d5c8bd7-2207-47fe-9b8b-c2b43fe30800\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"43cb7461-eedd-48a2-8964-dac0cede547d\\\"}\"]}]}],\"moreFiles\":0,\"changedFiles\":[\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174740__x7ef5ea/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174755__x531263/agent.out\",\"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174810__xbd1c73/agent.out\"]}},\"tool_result_meta\":[{\"id\":\"toolu_01HBNkUJsFznAUCGM7yg4qoV\",\"permission_decision\":{\"decision\":\"accept\",\"source\":\"config\",\"reason_type\":\"mode\"}}]}"," {\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-opus-5-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CggyoqYodYPpBmeLwAWoN\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01N2zXsDpzgXrob3iH2qjQdD\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"cd $HOME/.cache/plan-x193f88-research/hub/repo && sed -n 1,40p docs/curation-2026-09-28.md; sed -n 235,260p README.md\",\"description\":\"Read hub curation notes about CDN bundles and README limits\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":1666,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":160737,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":1666},\"output_tokens\":16,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"global\",\"speed\":\"standard\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"4c67436b-08b0-4220-8f4a-c880df6e2d31\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-11-04T00:58:03.224Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CggyoqL9TVm7RGKPmGKf9\",\"wire_tool_inputs\":{\"toolu_01N2zXsDpzgXrob3iH2qjQdD\":{\"command\":\"cd $HOME/.cache/plan-x193f88-research/hub/repo && sed -n 1,40p docs/curation-2026-09-28.md; sed -n 235,260p README.md\",\"description\":\"Read hub curation notes about CDN bundles and README limits\"}}}","+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01N2zXsDpzgXrob3iH2qjQdD\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"# Library import — 28 Sep 2026\\n\\n`C:\\\\dev\\\\GPT-games` held 336 game pages and 4 source zips, already renamed by\\nsource (its own `SOURCE-REVIEW.md` explains the source guesses). The wall held\\n245 games. Every file on both sides was compared, and each game now appears\\nonce, in its newest version, under the library's naming convention\\n(`Source-Title-YYYY-MM-DD-model.html`, see the README).\\n\\n**342** games in the catalogue · **104** new (98 on the wall, 6 hidden) · **244** kept and renamed · **7** left out\\n\\n## How the two sides were matched\\n\\n1. **Byte-identical** (SHA-256): 149 files. The wall's file was renamed to the folder's name.\\n2. **Same title, same game code**: 74 files. The folder's copy is an offline\\n   bundle of the same build: the libraries a page loads from a CDN (three.js,\\n   Babylon.js, React) are inlined as base64, and the code is re-emitted by a\\n   bundler. The bundle adds no game text of its own, only library code, so they\\n   are one version of one game. The wall keeps its lean build, renamed:\\n   *HOT TREADS* is 115 KB on the wall and 22.8 MB bundled.\\n   Project folders (Aetherfall, Pennywing, Runeclash…) stay folders.\\n3. **Same title, the wall's build is newer**: kept the wall's build, renamed.\\n   - Little World — Sing, play, grow — hub build is newer (voice storage schema v2 vs v1)\\n   - Plus One — A life of your own — hub build has session content the GPT copy lacks\\n   - Singularity Tycoon — A history of intelligence — hub build has lessons and win conditions the GPT copy lacks\\n4. **Different titles, one lineage**: text shared between files (with library\\n   strings discounted) found the few renamed iterations; each was read to see\\n   which is newer.\\n5. **Everything else is a separate game** — including same-idea attempts whose\\n   code is unrelated (the two BLACKWELLs, Kinetic and Kinetic Studio, Form and\\n   Form Lab, the Endless Sky and Final Fantasy sets), as in the first curation.\\n\\n## Left out\\n\\n| File | Why |\\n|---|---|\\n| `Daytona-USA-Days-of-Daytona-USA-Rival-Battle-II-2026-09-07-model-unknown.html` | older build (v5.0) of Days of Daytona USA; the wall keeps v12.0, the audited build |\\n| `Out-Run-RUNOUT-The-coast-is-calling-2026-09-07-model-unknown.html` | older iteration of SUPER RUNOUT (2026-09-11), which is on the wall |\\n| `Star-Fox-Vanguard-Wing-2026-09-10-model-unknown.html` | a \\\"Boot page ready.\\\" placeholder (Milestone 0), not a game |\\n| `original-Hudson-s-little-kitchen-Learn-together-2026-09-17-model-unknown.html` | superseded by Hudson's little home, which is the kitchen plus a family room |\\n| `original-Mandel-A-voxel-fractal-explorer-Attempt-01-2026-09-12-model-unknown.html` | earlier build of Mandel 3D (same code, before the orbit camera) |\\nin and hitting reload is the whole loop. (It remembers each file's parsed head\\nuntil the file changes, so that stays instant at four hundred games.)\\n\\n```bash\\npnpm test         # parsers, layout rules, zip reading, search and filters, Couch and Catalogue logic\\npnpm scan         # rebuild data/games.json by hand; --list prints every game\\npnpm dev --host 0.0.0.0   # reach it from your phone on the same wifi\\n```\\n\\nThe scan's output is worth a glance after a big import. Past forty games it\\nprints a summary instead of every title, followed by anything that needs you:\\nfiles too large for GitHub, projects that still load files from the site root,\\nproject folders whose extra pages might really be separate games.\\n\\n## Playing\\n\\nClicking a cabinet runs the game **inside** the hub, so leaving it puts you back\\non the wall with your scroll position, search and filters exactly as you left\\nthem. Nothing is written into a game file to make that work — the hub only\\nattaches listeners to the game's document, which it is allowed to do because\\nthe games are served from the same origin.\\n\\nThe bar in the corner has three buttons: **←** back to the wall, **🎲** roll\\nanother random game from what the wall was showing, and **✕**. A tap of ✕\\nfolds the bar down to just the ✕ (tap again to bring it back); holding it\\nremoves the bar entirely until the hub is reloaded. The browser's Back button\\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174737__x193f88/work\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"041395ab-5146-4633-b27b-c7bc1bdf7a40\",\"uuid\":\"da6c38cf-a66a-4e13-b55