{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Pvtix7eZxBuEN2hHqGN1gu","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t/*!\n2\tmy-3D2dge module ARCADE v0.85.2: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode\n3\thttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\n4\tLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n5\t\n6\tWhat every coin-op had around its game: for arcade games, shooters, puzzles, pinball and brawlers.\n7\t- const cab = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'maze', lives: 3, extra: [10000] (or every: 20000), credits: null (free play;\n8\t  a number: coins a game, cab.coin() adds one), hud: true }); cab.start(players, { demo }) begins a game (one or two\n9\t  taking turns; false without the credits); cab.p is the player up ({ n, score, lives, save }), cab.players all.\n10\t- cab.add(points, at): the score (at: a world point { x, y, z }: the points float up there), an extra life at each\n11\t  threshold. cab.die() takes a life: 'again', 'next' (the other player's turn: \"PLAYER 2, READY!\"; keep each one's\n12\t  stage in p.save) or 'over'; then cab.continue(10, done) counts down (done(true): lives back, the score kept).\n13\t- Tables, saved per game and mode: cab.table(mode) (the top ten { name, score }), cab.qualifies(score, mode),\n14\t  cab.enter(score, mode, done): initials on a letter wheel (up and down turn it, left and right move, confirm takes a\n15\t  letter; taps on its arrows and OK do each); cab.entry is it while open. cab.drawTable(r, mode, y, title).\n16\t- cab.card('STAGE 2', 2) shows a card (cab.carding while one is up), cab.say('READY!') a word under it.\n17\t- The attract mode, on the title: cab.attract(dt) -> 'title', then 'demo' once o.idle seconds (20) pass without input\n18\t  (play the game's own bot, start(1, { demo: true }): DEMO shows, no table), 'scores' for o.scores seconds (6) once\n19\t  cab.endDemo() is called or o.demo seconds (30) pass, then 'title'; any input goes back to 'title'.\n20\t- cab.update(dt) every step (cards, the entry, the continue); cab.draw(r, [x, y, w, h]) after your drawing: the HUD\n21\t  (in the playfield's box: the screen when none), cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry.\n22\t\n23\t```js arcade\n24\tconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }), cab = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'doc', lives: 2, extra: [500] });\n25\tcab.start(1); cab.add(300); cab.add(300);\n26\tif (cab.p.score !== 600 || cab.p.lives !== 3) throw new Error('extra life');\n27\tif (cab.die() !== 'again' || cab.die() !== 'again' || cab.die() !== 'over') throw new Error('lives');\n28\tcab.start(2); if (cab.die() !== 'next' || cab.p.n !== 2) throw new Error('turns');\n29\t```\n30\tRules: tables live in E.store ('arcade:' + id + ':' + mode; kept for the visit where storage is blocked); a demo is the game's own bot (or a recorded input log)\n31\tplaying the real rules; the entry and the continue read the game's keys, so hold play while either is open.\n32\t*/\n33\t(function (E) {\n34\t'use strict';\n35\tif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module ARCADE: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n36\t\n37\t/* =============================================================================\n38\t * ARCADE  scores, tables, initials, lives, credits, turns, cards and the attract mode\n39\t * ========================================================================== */\n40\tconst LETTERS = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.-! ', COLS = ['#ff4a4a', '#ffffff', '#ffe070'];\n41\tconst clicked = I => I.clicked ? I.clicked() : null;   // (a tap: the full engine's; the agent edition has none)\n42\tconst KEPT = {};   // the tables this visit, beside E.store (they still show where storage is blocked)\n43\tclass Arcade {\n44\t  /** new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points),\n45\t   *  credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds),\n46\t   *  hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] }) */\n47\t  constructor(game, o = {}) {\n48\t    /** game: the game it serves; id: the game's name (its tables'); o: the options */\n49\t    this.game = game; this.id = o.id || 'game'; this.o = Object.assign({ lives: 3, extra: [], credits: null, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6, hud: true, colors: COLS }, o);\n50\t    /** players: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the\n51\t     *  next extra life) }]; p: the player up; credits: coins in (null: free play); entry: the initials being entered\n52\t     *  ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null */\n53\t    this.players = []; this.p = null; this.credits = this.o.credits === null ? null : 0; this.entry = null;\n54\t    /** mode: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'; demo: a demo is playing (no table); phase: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' |\n55\t     *  'scores' */\n56\t    this.mode = 'title'; this.demo = false; this.phase = 'title';\n57\t    /** hi: the high score shown; wheel: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down,\n58\t     *  ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h] */\n59\t    this._cards = []; this._idle = 0; this._t = 0; this._cont = null; this.wheel = null; this.hi = 0;\n60\t  }\n61\t  /** begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a\n62\t   *  game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them */\n63\t  start(players = 1, o = {}) {\n64\t    if (this.credits !== null && !o.demo) { if (this.credits < this.o.credits) return false; this.credits -= this.o.credits; }\n65\t    this.players = Array.from({ length: Math.max(1, Math.min(2, players)) }, (_, i) => ({ n: i + 1, score: 0, lives: this.o.lives, save: null, next: this.o.every || (this.o.extra[0] === undefined ? Infinity : this.o.extra[0]) }));\n66\t    this.p = this.players[0]; this.mode = 'play'; this.demo = !!o.demo; this.entry = null; this._cont = null; this._cards.length = 0;\n67\t    this.hi = Math.max(this.hi, (this.table()[0] || { score: 0 }).score);\n68\t    if (this.players.length > 1) this.card('PLAYER 1', 1.6);\n69\t    return true;\n70\t  }"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ff8a465-a3dc-4463-ad61-3d7e016e47ef","uuid":"e81ef722-d44c-4295-9a51-06576652a779","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:58:57.919Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.cache/plan-x8534bd-wzXO/engine/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff/modules/arcade.js","content":"/*!\nmy-3D2dge module ARCADE v0.85.2: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode\nhttps://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge (MIT License)\nLoads after: the full engine or the agent edition. Needs: no other module.\n\nWhat every coin-op had around its game: for arcade games, shooters, puzzles, pinball and brawlers.\n- const cab = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'maze', lives: 3, extra: [10000] (or every: 20000), credits: null (free play;\n  a number: coins a game, cab.coin() adds one), hud: true }); cab.start(players, { demo }) begins a game (one or two\n  taking turns; false without the credits); cab.p is the player up ({ n, score, lives, save }), cab.players all.\n- cab.add(points, at): the score (at: a world point { x, y, z }: the points float up there), an extra life at each\n  threshold. cab.die() takes a life: 'again', 'next' (the other player's turn: \"PLAYER 2, READY!\"; keep each one's\n  stage in p.save) or 'over'; then cab.continue(10, done) counts down (done(true): lives back, the score kept).\n- Tables, saved per game and mode: cab.table(mode) (the top ten { name, score }), cab.qualifies(score, mode),\n  cab.enter(score, mode, done): initials on a letter wheel (up and down turn it, left and right move, confirm takes a\n  letter; taps on its arrows and OK do each); cab.entry is it while open. cab.drawTable(r, mode, y, title).\n- cab.card('STAGE 2', 2) shows a card (cab.carding while one is up), cab.say('READY!') a word under it.\n- The attract mode, on the title: cab.attract(dt) -> 'title', then 'demo' once o.idle seconds (20) pass without input\n  (play the game's own bot, start(1, { demo: true }): DEMO shows, no table), 'scores' for o.scores seconds (6) once\n  cab.endDemo() is called or o.demo seconds (30) pass, then 'title'; any input goes back to 'title'.\n- cab.update(dt) every step (cards, the entry, the continue); cab.draw(r, [x, y, w, h]) after your drawing: the HUD\n  (in the playfield's box: the screen when none), cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry.\n\n```js arcade\nconst E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true }), cab = new E.Arcade(game, { id: 'doc', lives: 2, extra: [500] });\ncab.start(1); cab.add(300); cab.add(300);\nif (cab.p.score !== 600 || cab.p.lives !== 3) throw new Error('extra life');\nif (cab.die() !== 'again' || cab.die() !== 'again' || cab.die() !== 'over') throw new Error('lives');\ncab.start(2); if (cab.die() !== 'next' || cab.p.n !== 2) throw new Error('turns');\n```\nRules: tables live in E.store ('arcade:' + id + ':' + mode; kept for the visit where storage is blocked); a demo is the game's own bot (or a recorded input log)\nplaying the real rules; the entry and the continue read the game's keys, so hold play while either is open.\n*/\n(function (E) {\n'use strict';\nif (!E) throw new Error('my-3D2dge module ARCADE: load engine/my-3d2dge.js (or the agent edition) first');\n\n/* =============================================================================\n * ARCADE  scores, tables, initials, lives, credits, turns, cards and the attract mode\n * ========================================================================== */\nconst LETTERS = 'ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789.-! ', COLS = ['#ff4a4a', '#ffffff', '#ffe070'];\nconst clicked = I => I.clicked ? I.clicked() : null;   // (a tap: the full engine's; the agent edition has none)\nconst KEPT = {};   // the tables this visit, beside E.store (they still show where storage is blocked)\nclass Arcade {\n  /** new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points),\n   *  credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds),\n   *  hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] }) */\n  constructor(game, o = {}) {\n    /** game: the game it serves; id: the game's name (its tables'); o: the options */\n    this.game = game; this.id = o.id || 'game'; this.o = Object.assign({ lives: 3, extra: [], credits: null, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6, hud: true, colors: COLS }, o);\n    /** players: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the\n     *  next extra life) }]; p: the player up; credits: coins in (null: free play); entry: the initials being entered\n     *  ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null */\n    this.players = []; this.p = null; this.credits = this.o.credits === null ? null : 0; this.entry = null;\n    /** mode: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'; demo: a demo is playing (no table); phase: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' |\n     *  'scores' */\n    this.mode = 'title'; this.demo = false; this.phase = 'title';\n    /** hi: the high score shown; wheel: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down,\n     *  ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h] */\n    this._cards = []; this._idle = 0; this._t = 0; this._cont = null; this.wheel = null; this.hi = 0;\n  }\n  /** begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a\n   *  game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them */\n  start(players = 1, o = {}) {\n    if (this.credits !== null && !o.demo) { if (this.credits < this.o.credits) return false; this.credits -= this.o.credits; }\n    this.players = Array.from({ length: Math.max(1, Math.min(2, players)) }, (_, i) => ({ n: i + 1, score: 0, lives: this.o.lives, save: null, next: this.o.every || (this.o.extra[0] === undefined ? Infinity : this.o.extra[0]) }));\n    this.p = this.players[0]; this.mode = 'play'; this.demo = !!o.demo; this.entry = null; this._cont = null; this._cards.length = 0;\n    this.hi = Math.max(this.hi, (this.table()[0] || { score: 0 }).score);\n    if (this.players.length > 1) this.card('PLAYER 1', 1.6);\n    return true;\n  }","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":215}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Pvtix7eZxBuEN2hHqGN1gu","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
