{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013keXMdA3ibVp1d1azZmdaL","type":"tool_result","content":"  1249 112570 PLAN.md\n# Karate Champon\n\n**Build plan for an original point-sparring karate game inspired by *Karate Champ* (1984).**\n\n> **Title:** *Karate Champon* is a riff on *Karate Champ*. Champon (ちゃんぽん) is Nagasaki's mixed noodle dish, and also Japanese slang for \"a mix of everything\". The title was picked as TASK.md asks: a silent brainstorm of 50 riffs on the source's name, then one pick with the OS's cryptographic RNG (`python3 -I` running `secrets.randbelow(50)`). It returned **#20 of 50: \"Karate Champon\"**. Use this title everywhere: the title screen, `<title>`, file names and the AI Hub catalogue.\n11:## 0. At a glance\n28:## 1. The source, and what we keep\n30:### 1.1 Research summary (what was confirmed)\n40:### 1.2 Design pillars (source trait → our mechanic)\n51:### 1.3 Narrative tone\n56:## 2. Game overview\n58:### 2.1 Core loop (write this sentence as a comment at the top of the game code)\n61:### 2.2 Modes (main menu)\n71:### 2.3 Story synopsis\n76:## 3. Controls and UX\n78:### 3.1 The twin-stick technique system (the heart of the game)\n99:### 3.2 Device mappings\n115:### 3.3 Prompts and glyphs\n126:### 3.4 10-foot rules (all screens)\n133:### 3.5 Touch-only devices\n140:## 4. Combat system\n142:### 4.1 Fighter body and stage geometry\n150:### 4.2 Technique table (authoritative data; frames are at 60 fps, and the engine steps at 120 Hz, so multiply by 2)\n188:### 4.3 Height and state rules\n196:### 4.4 Block\n202:### 4.5 Scoring a hit\n212:### 4.6 Simultaneous hits (*aiuchi*)\n215:### 4.7 Hit reactions\n220:### 4.8 Facing and cross-ups\n227:## 5. Bout rules and the referee\n229:### 5.1 Terms\n234:### 5.2 Bout state machine (`KC.Bout`, deterministic; all timings × `TUNE.refPace`)\n262:### 5.3 Referee and judges (`KC.Referee`)\n297:### 5.4 Fight HUD (drawn on the canvas in `r.overlay`, anchored to `r.W`/`r.H`)\n309:## 6. CPU AI (`KC.KarateAI`)\n311:### 6.1 Architecture\n328:### 6.2 Personalities\n342:### 6.3 Balance targets (asserted by `ai.test`, §18)\n349:## 7. Content\n351:### 7.1 Roster\n372:### 7.2 Stages (8 fight stages and 3 bonus locations)\n401:### 7.3 Champon Road (the story ladder, `KC.DATA.ladder`)\n428:### 7.4 Bonus stages\n452:### 7.5 Practice (Senpai's drill, `KC.Drill`)\n462:### 7.6 Items and objects\n465:### 7.7 Story beats\n470:## 8. Modes and screens (flow)\n482:### 8.1 Title\n488:### 8.2 Character select (versus)\n494:### 8.3 Champon Road screen\n498:### 8.4 Results (versus)\n501:### 8.5 Stage select\n504:### 8.6 Move List (pause item and DOJO)\n508:### 8.7 Continue, game over and initials\n513:### 8.8 Records\n516:### 8.9 Pause menu\n523:### 8.10 Options (game settings beside the engine's standard ones)\n536:### 8.11 About / Credits\n548:## 9. Art direction and assets\n550:### 9.1 Look\n565:### 9.2 Effects\n573:### 9.3 New art to make (by code)\n608:### 9.4 The bull (custom creature, `KC.Bull`)\n621:### 9.5 Palette and lighting\n626:## 10. Animation\n628:### 10.1 Base system\n631:### 10.2 New karate animations (EC7, or game-side rig post-processing)\n668:## 11. Audio (all generated in code, no files)\n670:### 11.1 Music\n693:### 11.2 Sound effects (`audio.define`)\n701:### 11.3 Gibberish voices (`KC.Voice`, an Animalese/Simlish-style synth on Web Audio)\n720:## 12. Multiplayer: local and AI Hub online\n722:### 12.1 Local\n726:### 12.2 AI Hub session protocol v1 (read `lib/hub/README.md` whole before M10)\n751:### 12.3 Roles\n756:### 12.4 Kachinuki rules online\n763:### 12.5 Messages (JSON, compact; ≤ 16 KB, ≤ 20 per second per copy)\n774:### 12.6 Netcode details\n789:## 13. Attract mode (`KC.Attract`)\n801:## 14. Dev mode (`KC.Dev`)\n841:## 15. Architecture and modules\n843:### 15.1 Folder layout (all dev files inside the dev folder; only the final HTML and `exit-interview.json` sit beside PLAN.md)\n860:### 15.2 Source files (each a fragment of one shared IIFE that starts `const E = My3D2dge`, `'use strict'`; the namespace is `const KC = {}`, exposed as `window.KC` for tests)\n897:### 15.3 Data schemas (designers extend the game by editing these; systems never hard-code content)\n905:### 15.4 Engine changes (keep a record in `engine/CHANGES.md`; rerun `node kits/test.mjs fighting arcade` after each one)\n915:### 15.5 Game configuration\n932:### 15.6 `game.debug` (for tests and the engine's tools)\n943:### 15.7 Build and bundle\n960:## 16. Build order and milestones\n981:## 17. Riskiest parts and how to de-risk them\n998:## 18. Testing plan\n1000:### 18.1 The one command\n1010:### 18.2 Headless suites (what each checks)\n1075:### 18.3 Browser suites (Playwright, the engine's pinned 1.63.0)\n1088:### 18.4 What only a person can judge (do it by eye, with screenshots and filmstrips)\n1093:## 19. Hand-off checklist (the build's final step)\n1095:### 19.1 Definition of done (from TASK.md)\n1102:### 19.2 About screen, chat reply and exit interview (one source: `data/about.json`)\n1132:### 19.3 Operational rules (from TASK.md; repeated here because they are easy to miss)\n1137:### 19.4 Requirements traceability\n1166:## Appendix A: Text (terse, ALL CAPS; voices are gibberish, these are the subtitles)\n1239:## Appendix B: Default input preset (`KC_KEYS`, single player)","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ff8a465-a3dc-4463-ad61-3d7e016e47ef","uuid":"13005d68-c4c2-4b7a-8aca-8a38c355eec4","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:31:48.588Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"  1249 112570 PLAN.md\n# Karate Champon\n\n**Build plan for an original point-sparring karate game inspired by *Karate Champ* (1984).**\n\n> **Title:** *Karate Champon* is a riff on *Karate Champ*. Champon (ちゃんぽん) is Nagasaki's mixed noodle dish, and also Japanese slang for \"a mix of everything\". The title was picked as TASK.md asks: a silent brainstorm of 50 riffs on the source's name, then one pick with the OS's cryptographic RNG (`python3 -I`