{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013UFfZtxwaqJN9Z6vfbqMyb","type":"tool_result","content":"843\t### 15.1 Folder layout (all dev files inside the dev folder; only the final HTML and `exit-interview.json` sit beside PLAN.md)\n844\t```\n845\tKarateChampon-KarateChamp1984-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174743/\n846\t  engine/            sparse copy of my-3d2dge dist/handoff (my-3d2dge.js, modules/, tools/, kits/, docs/, package.json) + CHANGES.md (every engine edit and why)\n847\t  vendor/aihub/      session.js (unmodified), harness.html, bridge.js, round.js (tests only)\n848\t  assets/            kc-set.js (cut store set) + kc-shapes.js (our E.SHAPES) + kc-sprites.js\n849\t  src/               game source fragments, concatenated in name order into one IIFE (§15.2)\n850\t  data/about.json    the About-screen text = the exit interview (§19)\n851\t  dev.html           dev page: session.js first in <head>, engine, assets, build/game.js\n852\t  build/game.js      generated\n853\t  tools/build.mjs    src → build/game.js (one IIFE, `node --check`), then bundle → ../KarateChampon-…html and ../exit-interview.json\n854\t  tests/run.mjs      THE test command (§18)\n855\t  tests/lib/*.mjs    loadGame (vm), fakeHub, autopilot helpers\n856\t  tests/*.test.mjs   suites\n857\t  tests/out/         screenshots, filmstrips (reviewed by eye only)\n858\t```\n859\t\n860\t### 15.2 Source files (each a fragment of one shared IIFE that starts `const E = My3D2dge`, `'use strict'`; the namespace is `const KC = {}`, exposed as `window.KC` for tests)\n861\t\n862\t| File | Responsibility |\n863\t|---|---|\n864\t| `00-header.js` | core-loop comment, version, `KC`, `TUNE_DEFAULTS`, live `TUNE` |\n865\t| `01-util.js` | rng streams, 4-way quantizer with hysteresis, easing, text sanitizer, number formatting |\n866\t| `02-data-techniques.js` | `KC.DATA.techniques` (§4.2) |\n867\t| `03-data-roster.js` | `KC.DATA.roster` (§7.1, §6.2), tips, voices, quotes, unlocks |\n868\t| `04-data-stages.js` | `KC.DATA.stages` (§7.2) |\n869\t| `05-data-ladder.js` | `KC.DATA.ladder`, `KC.DATA.lessons`, `KC.DATA.bonus` |\n870\t| `06-data-text.js` | every string (Appendix A), the call table in EN and JP, the hint pool |\n871\t| `07-validate.js` | `KC.validateData()`: ids resolve, numbers in range, every technique reachable in the matrix; runs at boot in dev and in tests |\n872\t| `10-input.js` | `KC.readControl(input, foeSide)`, the press-edge and upgrade window, P1/P2 key maps, `promptFor`, `KC.glyph` icon renderer, device tracking, touch-only gate |\n873\t| `11-poses.js` | karate poses, spins, flips, kime and the referee signals as rig post-processing or EC7 helpers |\n874\t| `20-voice.js` | `KC.Voice` synth, profiles, `speak(line, who) → seconds`, kiai, crowd |\n875\t| `21-music.js` | all songs and stings |\n876\t| `22-sfx.js` | `audio.define(...)` for every sfx in §11.2 |\n877\t| `30-karateka.js` | `KC.Karateka` (body, state machine, techniques, boxes, control, snapshot/apply, pose, draw) |\n878\t| `31-referee.js` | `KC.Referee` (actors, signals, calls queue, subtitles, judges, hantei votes) |\n879\t| `32-bout.js` | `KC.Bout` (§5.2 state machine, scoring, events, its own hit-stop, aiuchi window, stats) |\n880\t| `33-ai.js` | `KC.KarateAI` (perception, decisions, levels, personalities, showcase, habit tracker) |\n881\t| `34-hud.js` | fight HUD, popups, hints, input display, prompt bar |\n882\t| `35-stage.js` | stage painters (backdrop, floor, props, crowd, lights, weather, ambience), side and 2.5D |\n883\t| `36-crowd.js` | crowd silhouettes and front-row rigs, reactions, Mei cameo |\n884\t| `40-bonus-boards.js`, `41-bonus-pots.js`, `42-bonus-bull.js` | the three bonus stages (`KC.Bull` creature in 42) |\n885\t| `43-drill.js` | `KC.Drill` (Senpai's practice) and Free Spar |\n886\t| `50-scene-title.js` | title, main menu, touch gate, idle timer |\n887\t| `51-scene-attract.js` | `KC.Attract` director |\n888\t| `52-scene-road.js` | Champon Road screen, VS card, promotion, continue, game over, ending, credits, cutscene player |\n889\t| `53-scene-fight.js` | the `fight` scene for all modes (`data.mode`: story, versus, kachinuki, attract, freeSpar) |\n890\t| `54-scene-versus.js` | versus setup, `KC.Select`, stage select, results, local Kachinuki |\n891\t| `55-scene-misc.js` | dojo menu, bonus menu, records, about, move list, the `bonus` and `practice` scene wrappers |\n892\t| `60-online.js` | `KC.Net` (AIHub roles, card, messages, puppets, prediction, fairness delay) and `KC.Kachinuki` |\n893\t| `70-dev.js` | `KC.Dev` panel, overlays, Technique Lab scene, warp |\n894\t| `80-debug.js` | `game.debug` (§15.6), `game.stateHash` |\n895\t| `90-start.js` | `new E.Game(...)`, scene registry, boot steps, deep links, `game.start` |\n896\t\n897\t### 15.3 Data schemas (designers extend the game by editing these; systems never hard-code content)\n898\t- **technique:** `{ id, name, jp, input: [L, R], height: 'high'|'mid'|'low'|'none', f: [startup, active, recovery], travel: { x, phase }, air: { vz, vx } | null, reach: [min, max], pts: [lo, hi], unblockable, knockdown, closeAlt, closeGap, spin: 0 | .5 | 1, move: rigSpec, limb, hitR, kiai, bull, potHeights }`\n899\t- **fighter:** `{ id, name, title, rig, stats: { walk, reach, speed }, signature, ai: { level, aggression, patience, jump, block, gap, crouch, weights, habit }, voice: { f0, formant, rate, wave, rough, vib }, quotes: { intro, win, lose }, tip, unlock }`\n900\t- **stage:** `{ id, name, music, backdrop, floor: { mat, colors }, props: [[kind, id, x, y, z, opts]], lights: { ambient, list }, crowd: { rows, palette, front: [ids], mei }, weather, particles, ambience, arena: { x0: 0, x1: 400, marks: [150, 250] } }`\n901\t- **ladder node:** `{ kind: 'cutscene'|'practice'|'match'|'bonus'|'ending'|'credits', id, stage, opponent, lesson, bonus, promote, hints, script }`\n902\t- **lesson:** `{ id, title, stage, drills: [techId] }`. **bonus:** `{ id, kind: 'boards'|'pots'|'bull', stage, params }`.\n903\t- Adding an opponent, stage, lesson or bonus variant is a data edit plus `validateData()`. The Dev Warp tab lists any new nodes automatically.\n904\t\n905\t### 15.4 Engine changes (keep a record in `engine/CHANGES.md`; rerun `node kits/test.mjs fighting arcade` after each one)\n906\t- **EC1, right-stick codes.** `PadRAxisUp/Down/Left/Right` are pressed past 0.5 (on the dominant axis only, a 4-way gate) and released below 0.35. Their labels are 'R stick ↑' and so on, and they go in `FIXED_CODES`, like the left stick's `PadAxis*`. (Today the right stick exists only as `input.padAim` and cannot be bound or labelled; checked in `Input.tick`.)\n907\t- **EC2, standard-setting defaults.** `new E.Game({ defaults: { glyphs: 'playstation' } })` overrides a standard setting's default, and Restore defaults returns to it. (`STANDARD_SETTINGS` is internal and its glyphs default is `'auto'`.)\n908\t- **EC3, font glyphs.** Add ✕ ○ □ △ to the 5×7 font (`G57`).\n909\t- **EC4, live pause.** With `game.live = true`, `_step` keeps running timers and the scene's `update` while paused or while a menu screen is open. `game.paused` is still set, so the scene neutralizes local input. Needed for shared-world sessions, where a guest's menu must not stop the world.\n910\t- **EC5, voice bus.** `audio.bus('sfx'|'music'|'voice')` returns the GainNode. Add a standard **Voices** volume slider in Sound, honoured by mute.\n911\t- **EC6, Backdrop custom layers.** `{ kind: 'custom', parallax, draw(g, r, scrollX, layer) }`.\n912\t- **EC7, karate poses and moves.** Add `bow`, `seiza`, `kamae`, `yoi` and the block poses to the Humanoid's pose table, and the `kc_*` move specs to `E.MOVES`. If a change inside the rig proves risky, do it game-side by wrapping `rig.solvePose` (allowed and documented).\n913\t- **No change is needed for:** `menu.items` as a function (already supported); `E.Arcade`'s idle time (pass `idle: 10` if it is used; our own `KC.Attract` owns the 10 s rule); `E.FightStage` and `E.Platformer` (reused as they are). **Do not use `E.Match`, `E.Fighter`, `E.FightAI` or `game.freeze`:** they are built around life bars (SF2 rules), and `freeze` stalls `update`.\n914\t\n915\t### 15.5 Game configuration\n916\t```js\n917\tconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'side', bg: '#07060d', id: 'karate-champon',\n918\t  defaults: { glyphs: 'playstation' },                          // EC2\n919\t  autoPause: !AIHub.active,                                     // sessions never pause (EC4: game.live = AIHub.active)\n920\t  menu: { items: () => [...], settings: [...§8.10], controls: { tUp: 'Technique ↑ high', tDown: 'Technique ↓ low', tLeft: 'Technique ←', tRight: 'Technique →' }, quit: AIHub.active ? false : 'title' } });\n921\t```\n922\t- `AIHub` exists on the page because the session client defines it even outside sessions, but not in Node tests. Read it once as `const HUB = typeof AIHub !== 'undefined' ? AIHub : null`; tests inject a fake.\n923\t- Scenes set `view: 'side'`, `views: ['side', 'brawler']` (fight scenes only; the `camera` setting picks one) and `input: KC_KEYS`. They are `pausable: true` in gameplay (not in sessions) and set `camera: { zoom: false }` and `touch: []`.\n924\t- **Boot steps** (`game.start({ boot: { title: 'KARATE CHAMPON', steps } })`):\n925\t  1. \"Sweeping the dojo floor\" (`validateData`);\n926\t  2. \"Folding the gi\" (build the rigs);\n927\t  3. \"Simmering the broth\" (sfx and music);\n928\t  4. \"Tuning the referee's whistle\" (voice profiles);\n929\t  5. \"Raking the gravel\" (stage caches).\n930\t- **Deep links:** `#title`, `#road/<node>`, `#fight/<stage>/<opponent>`, `#versus`, `#kachinuki/<n>`, `#bonus/<id>`, `#practice/<lesson>`, `#lab/<techId>`, `#attract`, `#about`, `#ending`. These are for `tools/check.mjs` and `filmstrip.mjs`.\n931\t\n932\t### 15.6 `game.debug` (for tests and the engine's tools)\n933\t- `snapshot()` returns:\n934\t```js\n935\t{ scene, mode, node, rank, score, settings: { difficulty, calls },\n936\t  bout: { phase, clock, points, roundWins, round, lastCall, lastPoint, fighters: [{ id, x, z, state, tech, phase, facing }] },\n937\t  bonus: { kind, state, points, objectsLeft }, drill: { lesson, index, result },\n938\t  attract: { step, t }, online: { role, me, queue, standings }, dev: { on, tuneChanged } }\n939\t```\n940\t- Helpers: `warp(nodeOrScene)`, `setTune(k, v)`, `resetTune()`, `control(side, ctrl)` (inject an intent), `autopilot(side, level | false)`, `exportTuning()`, `forceCall(id)`.\n941\t- `game.stateHash = () => [...fighters' x, z, state, tech, the bout phase, clock, points]` for the engine's replay tool.\n942\t\n943\t### 15.7 Build and bundle\n944\t- `node tools/build.mjs`:\n945\t  1. Concatenate `src/*.js` into one IIFE in `build/game.js` and check it with `node --check`.\n946\t  2. Write `../KarateChampon-KarateChamp1984-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174743.html`:\n947\t     - `<meta charset>`;\n948\t     - `session.js` inline and **byte-identical** (the test compares its hash with `vendor/aihub/session.js`);\n949\t     - viewport, `<title>Karate Champon</title>`, the description and the hub metas;\n950\t     - `<style>`;\n951\t     - the `E.bootSplash('KARATE CHAMPON')` markup;\n952\t     - `<canvas id=\"screen\">`;\n953\t     - then inline `<script>`s: the engine, the assets, the game.\n954\t  3. Escape `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script`.\n955\t  4. Write `../exit-interview.json` from `data/about.json` and validate it with `JSON.parse`.\n956\t- The final page makes **no external requests**. `tools/check.mjs` reports `external`, and the test asserts it is empty.\n957\t\n958\t---\n959\t\n960\t## 16. Build order and milestones\n961\tEach milestone ends with its tests green (`node tests/run.mjs --only <suites>`) and a playable build. Do them in order. Each depends on the ones before it, and the riskiest feel-defining work comes first.\n962\t\n963\t| M | Deliverable | Exit criteria |\n964\t|---|---|---|\n965\t| **M0 Setup** | dev folder; sparse engine copy (`git clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git` then `git sparse-checkout set dist/handoff`, ≈16 MB); `curl` the 4 hub files (never clone ai-hub: it is 5.3 GB); `npm install` and `npx playwright install chromium` in `engine/`; `build.mjs`; the `run.mjs` skeleton; `dev.html` with an empty title | `node kits/test.mjs fighting arcade` passes; `run.mjs` prints `0 failed` |\n966\t| **M1 Input and Karateka core** | EC1, EC3; `KC.readControl`, glyph icons; Karateka with walk, jump, crouch and the 4 standing techniques; joint boxes; the Technique Lab scene | `input.test` passes; the 4 techniques land in the Lab |\n967\t| **M2 Full moveset** | all 15 techniques plus block, flips, roll and pivot; EC7 poses; spins and flips; filmstrips reviewed | `technique.test` passes (reach ±4 u, height rules, block, counter, aiuchi) |\n968\t| **M3 Bout, referee and HUD** | `KC.Bout`, `KC.Referee` (text calls first), judges and hantei, HUD; the `fight` scene vs a dummy | `bout.test` passes; a quick bout plays start to finish in the browser |\n969\t| **M4 AI** | `KC.KarateAI`, personalities, levels, showcase, Autopilot | `ai.test` passes (completes, deterministic, level ordering, coverage) |\n970\t| **M5 Stages and art** | EC6; the 8 stages and 3 bonus locations; crowds; custom shapes and sprites; lights; the 2.5D view | screenshot review of every stage in both views; `tools/check.mjs` look notes addressed |\n971\t| **M6 Bonus and drills** | Boards, Pots, Bull (with the creature), `KC.Drill`, Free Spar | `bonus.test`, `drill.test` pass |\n972\t| **M7 Story and presentation** | title, main menu, Champon Road, VS cards, cutscenes, promotions, continue, game over, ending, credits, `E.Arcade` tables and initials, saves, unlocks, options, About (text placeholders are forbidden: write the real about text at M12 from `data/about.json`) | `story.test` (scripted full playthrough) passes |\n973\t| **M8 Audio** | EC5; `KC.Voice`; all music and sfx; crowd; wire them into the bus events | `audio.test` passes; listen pass in the browser |\n974\t| **M9 Local multiplayer** | versus setup, select, stage select, results, P2 keyboard/pad maps, local Kachinuki | `versus.test` passes |\n975\t| **M10 Online** | EC4; `KC.Net` with all roles; the card; puppets; prediction; fairness delay; Kachinuki; leave, time-up, end | `online.test` (fake hub) passes, then **the real harness passes** (2p; 4p with latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5; host-leave; server) |\n976\t| **M11 Attract, touch gate and dev** | `KC.Attract`, the touch-only gate, the full dev panel and warps | `attract.test`, `dev.test`, `ui.test` pass |\n977\t| **M12 Polish and ship** | juice and balance passes (Autopilot win-rate table), comfort, a final look review, About text plus `exit-interview.json`, the bundle, **a full manual playthrough**, a no-TODO scan | the full `node tests/run.mjs` prints `0 failed`; the bundle opens from `file://` with no errors; `grep -nE \"TODO|FIXME|XXX|placeholder\"` over `src/` finds nothing |\n978\t\n979\t---\n980\t\n981\t## 17. Riskiest parts and how to de-risk them\n982\t\n983\t| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risking (when) |\n984\t|---|---|---|\n985\t| **Karate animations** (spins, back kicks, somersaults, blocks) | `E.MOVES` has no karate-specific techniques; rig spins and airborne flips are unproven | Build the **Technique Lab in M1**, before any content. Prototype the Back Kick and the Front Somersault first. Spin by animating the 3D rig's facing angle. Fallbacks, in order: joint post-processing around the hips (Emberdeep), then a cut mocap clip. Review filmstrips for every technique |\n986\t| **Fair, readable hit detection** | Joint-derived boxes make outcomes depend on animation tuning | The explicit height rules (§4.3) on top of joint boxes; the Lab's **measured gap** vs the table (±4 u, asserted); dev box overlays; quality computed from data, not pixels |\n987\t| **Twin-stick on keyboard feels awkward** | Two-hand chords and keyboard rollover | The WASD + IJKL layout; the 4-frame posture upgrade window; the 0.15 s buffer; face buttons as an alternative; drills that teach it; input display. Test with real keyboards in M1–M3 |\n988\t| **Netplay feel under latency** | Host authority, the 20 msg/s cap, 150 ms latency in the hub test | Deliberate, slow techniques (the source's pace) forgive latency. Add the fairness delay and guest wind-up prediction. **Build the fake hub with latency, jitter and loss at the start of M10** and measure input-to-response time (target ≤ 250 ms at 150 ms one-way). Fallback: a uniform input delay for both sides |\n989\t| **AI quality and exploits** | The source's CPU was exploitable (a TAS found fixed reactions) | Seeded CPU-vs-CPU and Autopilot balance tables in `ai.test`; habit trackers at L8+; mistakes and reaction curves; live dev sliders |\n990\t| **Scope** | 9 matches, 11 locations, 3 bonus games, 3 lessons, story, versus, Kachinuki, online, attract, dev, voices | Data-driven content (§15.3). One `Bout` and one `Karateka` power every mode (story, versus, Kachinuki, online, attract, drills). A vertical slice is playable at M3 |\n991\t| **Hub harness conformance** | The card answers, server mode, time-up grace, traffic both ways, host-leave void | Follow `examples/arena.html`'s structure. Run the real harness headless with Playwright in the test command (§18.3) as soon as M10 starts, with a stub world |\n992\t| **The engine's pause and hit-stop stop `update`** | That stalls networking and makes slow motion change send rates | EC4 live pause; the Bout's own hit-stop; real-time network cadence |\n993\t| **Single-file bundling** | Inline scripts can contain `</script`; the session client must stay unmodified | The build escapes `</script` and a test compares the session client's bytes; the test loads the bundle from `file://` and checks errors |\n994\t| **Environment** | `/tmp` here is a nearly full shared tmpfs (a clone failed with \"No space left on device\"); ports and processes are shared | Keep downloads and caches inside the dev folder; never clone ai-hub; serve with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` from `vendor/aihub` + the bundle, parse the printed port, fetch the game URL and check for `<title>Karate Champon` before trusting a result, and kill only that PID |\n995\t\n996\t---\n997\t\n998\t## 18. Testing plan\n999\t\n1000\t### 18.1 The one command\n1001\t`node tests/run.mjs` (from the dev folder) builds first, then runs every suite. It **prints only failing checks** (name and detail) and one final line:\n1002\t`KC TESTS: 412 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (38.2 s)`"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6ff8a465-a3dc-4463-ad61-3d7e016e47ef","uuid":"89cd7547-04ca-4819-b095-3953a163b9f0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:32:27.995Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174743__x8534bd/work/PLAN.md","content":"### 15.1 Folder layout (all dev files inside the dev folder; only the final HTML and `exit-interview.json` sit beside PLAN.md)\n```\nKarateChampon-KarateChamp1984-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174743/\n  engine/            sparse copy of my-3d2dge dist/handoff (my-3d2dge.js, modules/, tools/, kits/, docs/, package.json) + CHANGES.md (every engine edit and why)\n  vendor/aihub/      session.js (unmodified), harness.html, bridge.js, round.js (tests only)\n  assets/            kc-set.js (cut store set) + kc-shapes.js (our E.SHAPES) + kc-sprites.js\n  src/               game source fragments, concatenated in name order into one IIFE (§15.2)\n  data/about.json    the About-screen text = the exit interview (§19)\n  dev.html           dev page: session.js first in <head>, engine, assets, build/game.js\n  build/game.js      generated\n  tools/build.mjs    src → build/game.js (one IIFE, `node --check`), then bundle → ../KarateChampon-…html and ../exit-interview.json\n  tests/run.mjs      THE test command (§18)\n  tests/lib/*.mjs    loadGame (vm), fakeHub, autopilot helpers\n  tests/*.test.mjs   suites\n  tests/out/         screenshots, filmstrips (reviewed by eye only)\n```\n\n### 15.2 Source files (each a fragment of one shared IIFE that starts `const E = My3D2dge`, `'use strict'`; the namespace is `const KC = {}`, exposed as `window.KC` for tests)\n\n| File | Responsibility |\n|---|---|\n| `00-header.js` | core-loop comment, version, `KC`, `TUNE_DEFAULTS`, live `TUNE` |\n| `01-util.js` | rng streams, 4-way quantizer with hysteresis, easing, text sanitizer, number formatting |\n| `02-data-techniques.js` | `KC.DATA.techniques` (§4.2) |\n| `03-data-roster.js` | `KC.DATA.roster` (§7.1, §6.2), tips, voices, quotes, unlocks |\n| `04-data-stages.js` | `KC.DATA.stages` (§7.2) |\n| `05-data-ladder.js` | `KC.DATA.ladder`, `KC.DATA.lessons`, `KC.DATA.bonus` |\n| `06-data-text.js` | every string (Appendix A), the call table in EN and JP, the hint pool |\n| `07-validate.js` | `KC.validateData()`: ids resolve, numbers in range, every technique reachable in the matrix; runs at boot in dev and in tests |\n| `10-input.js` | `KC.readControl(input, foeSide)`, the press-edge and upgrade window, P1/P2 key maps, `promptFor`, `KC.glyph` icon renderer, device tracking, touch-only gate |\n| `11-poses.js` | karate poses, spins, flips, kime and the referee signals as rig post-processing or EC7 helpers |\n| `20-voice.js` | `KC.Voice` synth, profiles, `speak(line, who) → seconds`, kiai, crowd |\n| `21-music.js` | all songs and stings |\n| `22-sfx.js` | `audio.define(...)` for every sfx in §11.2 |\n| `30-karateka.js` | `KC.Karateka` (body, state machine, techniques, boxes, control, snapshot/apply, pose, draw) |\n| `31-referee.js` | `KC.Referee` (actors, signals, calls queue, subtitles, judges, hantei votes) |\n| `32-bout.js` | `KC.Bout` (§5.2 state machine, scoring, events, its own hit-stop, aiuchi window, stats) |\n| `33-ai.js` | `KC.KarateAI` (perception, decisions, levels, personalities, showcase, habit tracker) |\n| `34-hud.js` | fight HUD, popups, hints, input display, prompt bar |\n| `35-stage.js` | stage painters (backdrop, floor, props, crowd, lights, weather, ambience), side and 2.5D |\n| `36-crowd.js` | crowd silhouettes and front-row rigs, reactions, Mei cameo |\n| `40-bonus-boards.js`, `41-bonus-pots.js`, `42-bonus-bull.js` | the three bonus stages (`KC.Bull` creature in 42) |\n| `43-drill.js` | `KC.Drill` (Senpai's practice) and Free Spar |\n| `50-scene-title.js` | title, main menu, touch gate, idle timer |\n| `51-scene-attract.js` | `KC.Attract` director |\n| `52-scene-road.js` | Champon Road screen, VS card, promotion, continue, game over, ending, credits, cutscene player |\n| `53-scene-fight.js` | the `fight` scene for all modes (`data.mode`: story, versus, kachinuki, attract, freeSpar) |\n| `54-scene-versus.js` | versus setup, `KC.Select`, stage select, results, local Kachinuki |\n| `55-scene-misc.js` | dojo menu, bonus menu, records, about, move list, the `bonus` and `practice` scene wrappers |\n| `60-online.js` | `KC.Net` (AIHub roles, card, messages, puppets, prediction, fairness delay) and `KC.Kachinuki` |\n| `70-dev.js` | `KC.Dev` panel, overlays, Technique Lab scene, warp |\n| `80-debug.js` | `game.debug` (§15.6), `game.stateHash` |\n| `90-start.js` | `new E.Game(...)`, scene registry, boot steps, deep links, `game.start` |\n\n### 15.3 Data schemas (designers extend the game by editing these; systems never hard-code content)\n- **technique:** `{ id, name, jp, input: [L, R], height: 'high'|'mid'|'low'|'none', f: [startup, active, recovery], travel: { x, phase }, air: { vz, vx } | null, reach: [min, max], pts: [lo, hi], unblockable, knockdown, closeAlt, closeGap, spin: 0 | .5 | 1, move: rigSpec, limb, hitR, kiai, bull, potHeights }`\n- **fighter:** `{ id, name, title, rig, stats: { walk, reach, speed }, signature, ai: { level, aggression, patience, jump, block, gap, crouch, weights, habit }, voice: { f0, formant, rate, wave, rough, vib }, quotes: { intro, win, lose }, tip, unlock }`\n- **stage:** `{ id, name, music, backdrop, floor: { mat, colors }, props: [[kind, id, x, y, z, opts]], lights: { ambient, list }, crowd: { rows, palette, front: [ids], mei }, weather, particles, ambience, arena: { x0: 0, x1: 400, marks: [150, 250] } }`\n- **ladder node:** `{ kind: 'cutscene'|'practice'|'match'|'bonus'|'ending'|'credits', id, stage, opponent, lesson, bonus, promote, hints, script }`\n- **lesson:** `{ id, title, stage, drills: [techId] }`. **bonus:** `{ id, kind: 'boards'|'pots'|'bull', stage, params }`.\n- Adding an opponent, stage, lesson or bonus variant is a data edit plus `validateData()`. The Dev Warp tab lists any new nodes automatically.\n\n### 15.4 Engine changes (keep a record in `engine/CHANGES.md`; rerun `node kits/test.mjs fighting arcade` after each one)\n- **EC1, right-stick codes.** `PadRAxisUp/Down/Left/Right` are pressed past 0.5 (on the dominant axis only, a 4-way gate) and released below 0.35. Their labels are 'R stick ↑' and so on, and they go in `FIXED_CODES`, like the left stick's `PadAxis*`. (Today the right stick exists only as `input.padAim` and cannot be bound or labelled; checked in `Input.tick`.)\n- **EC2, standard-setting defaults.** `new E.Game({ defaults: { glyphs: 'playstation' } })` overrides a standard setting's default, and Restore defaults returns to it. (`STANDARD_SETTINGS` is internal and its glyphs default is `'auto'`.)\n- **EC3, font glyphs.** Add ✕ ○ □ △ to the 5×7 font (`G57`).\n- **EC4, live pause.** With `game.live = true`, `_step` keeps running timers and the scene's `update` while paused or while a menu screen is open. `game.paused` is still set, so the scene neutralizes local input. Needed for shared-world sessions, where a guest's menu must not stop the world.\n- **EC5, voice bus.** `audio.bus('sfx'|'music'|'voice')` returns the GainNode. Add a standard **Voices** volume slider in Sound, honoured by mute.\n- **EC6, Backdrop custom layers.** `{ kind: 'custom', parallax, draw(g, r, scrollX, layer) }`.\n- **EC7, karate poses and moves.** Add `bow`, `seiza`, `kamae`, `yoi` and the block poses to the Humanoid's pose table, and the `kc_*` move specs to `E.MOVES`. If a change inside the rig proves risky, do it game-side by wrapping `rig.solvePose` (allowed and documented).\n- **No change is needed for:** `menu.items` as a function (already supported); `E.Arcade`'s idle time (pass `idle: 10` if it is used; our own `KC.Attract` owns the 10 s rule); `E.FightStage` and `E.Platformer` (reused as they are). **Do not use `E.Match`, `E.Fighter`, `E.FightAI` or `game.freeze`:** they are built around life bars (SF2 rules), and `freeze` stalls `update`.\n\n### 15.5 Game configuration\n```js\nconst game = new E.Game({ canvas: 'screen', res: 'ps1', expand: true, view: 'side', bg: '#07060d', id: 'karate-champon',\n  defaults: { glyphs: 'playstation' },                          // EC2\n  autoPause: !AIHub.active,                                     // sessions never pause (EC4: game.live = AIHub.active)\n  menu: { items: () => [...], settings: [...§8.10], controls: { tUp: 'Technique ↑ high', tDown: 'Technique ↓ low', tLeft: 'Technique ←', tRight: 'Technique →' }, quit: AIHub.active ? false : 'title' } });\n```\n- `AIHub` exists on the page because the session client defines it even outside sessions, but not in Node tests. Read it once as `const HUB = typeof AIHub !== 'undefined' ? AIHub : null`; tests inject a fake.\n- Scenes set `view: 'side'`, `views: ['side', 'brawler']` (fight scenes only; the `camera` setting picks one) and `input: KC_KEYS`. They are `pausable: true` in gameplay (not in sessions) and set `camera: { zoom: false }` and `touch: []`.\n- **Boot steps** (`game.start({ boot: { title: 'KARATE CHAMPON', steps } })`):\n  1. \"Sweeping the dojo floor\" (`validateData`);\n  2. \"Folding the gi\" (build the rigs);\n  3. \"Simmering the broth\" (sfx and music);\n  4. \"Tuning the referee's whistle\" (voice profiles);\n  5. \"Raking the gravel\" (stage caches).\n- **Deep links:** `#title`, `#road/<node>`, `#fight/<stage>/<opponent>`, `#versus`, `#kachinuki/<n>`, `#bonus/<id>`, `#practice/<lesson>`, `#lab/<techId>`, `#attract`, `#about`, `#ending`. These are for `tools/check.mjs` and `filmstrip.mjs`.\n\n### 15.6 `game.debug` (for tests and the engine's tools)\n- `snapshot()` returns:\n```js\n{ scene, mode, node, rank, score, settings: { difficulty, calls },\n  bout: { phase, clock, points, roundWins, round, lastCall, lastPoint, fighters: [{ id, x, z, state, tech, phase, facing }] },\n  bonus: { kind, state, points, objectsLeft }, drill: { lesson, index, result },\n  attract: { step, t }, online: { role, me, queue, standings }, dev: { on, tuneChanged } }\n```\n- Helpers: `warp(nodeOrScene)`, `setTune(k, v)`, `resetTune()`, `control(side, ctrl)` (inject an intent), `autopilot(side, level | false)`, `exportTuning()`, `forceCall(id)`.\n- `game.stateHash = () => [...fighters' x, z, state, tech, the bout phase, clock, points]` for the engine's replay tool.\n\n### 15.7 Build and bundle\n- `node tools/build.mjs`:\n  1. Concatenate `src/*.js` into one IIFE in `build/game.js` and check it with `node --check`.\n  2. Write `../KarateChampon-KarateChamp1984-claude-opus-5-5-max-20261103-174743.html`:\n     - `<meta charset>`;\n     - `session.js` inline and **byte-identical** (the test compares its hash with `vendor/aihub/session.js`);\n     - viewport, `<title>Karate Champon</title>`, the description and the hub metas;\n     - `<style>`;\n     - the `E.bootSplash('KARATE CHAMPON')` markup;\n     - `<canvas id=\"screen\">`;\n     - then inline `<script>`s: the engine, the assets, the game.\n  3. Escape `</script` inside inlined code as `<\\/script`.\n  4. Write `../exit-interview.json` from `data/about.json` and validate it with `JSON.parse`.\n- The final page makes **no external requests**. `tools/check.mjs` reports `external`, and the test asserts it is empty.\n\n---\n\n## 16. Build order and milestones\nEach milestone ends with its tests green (`node tests/run.mjs --only <suites>`) and a playable build. Do them in order. Each depends on the ones before it, and the riskiest feel-defining work comes first.\n\n| M | Deliverable | Exit criteria |\n|---|---|---|\n| **M0 Setup** | dev folder; sparse engine copy (`git clone --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --sparse https://github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge.git` then `git sparse-checkout set dist/handoff`, ≈16 MB); `curl` the 4 hub files (never clone ai-hub: it is 5.3 GB); `npm install` and `npx playwright install chromium` in `engine/`; `build.mjs`; the `run.mjs` skeleton; `dev.html` with an empty title | `node kits/test.mjs fighting arcade` passes; `run.mjs` prints `0 failed` |\n| **M1 Input and Karateka core** | EC1, EC3; `KC.readControl`, glyph icons; Karateka with walk, jump, crouch and the 4 standing techniques; joint boxes; the Technique Lab scene | `input.test` passes; the 4 techniques land in the Lab |\n| **M2 Full moveset** | all 15 techniques plus block, flips, roll and pivot; EC7 poses; spins and flips; filmstrips reviewed | `technique.test` passes (reach ±4 u, height rules, block, counter, aiuchi) |\n| **M3 Bout, referee and HUD** | `KC.Bout`, `KC.Referee` (text calls first), judges and hantei, HUD; the `fight` scene vs a dummy | `bout.test` passes; a quick bout plays start to finish in the browser |\n| **M4 AI** | `KC.KarateAI`, personalities, levels, showcase, Autopilot | `ai.test` passes (completes, deterministic, level ordering, coverage) |\n| **M5 Stages and art** | EC6; the 8 stages and 3 bonus locations; crowds; custom shapes and sprites; lights; the 2.5D view | screenshot review of every stage in both views; `tools/check.mjs` look notes addressed |\n| **M6 Bonus and drills** | Boards, Pots, Bull (with the creature), `KC.Drill`, Free Spar | `bonus.test`, `drill.test` pass |\n| **M7 Story and presentation** | title, main menu, Champon Road, VS cards, cutscenes, promotions, continue, game over, ending, credits, `E.Arcade` tables and initials, saves, unlocks, options, About (text placeholders are forbidden: write the real about text at M12 from `data/about.json`) | `story.test` (scripted full playthrough) passes |\n| **M8 Audio** | EC5; `KC.Voice`; all music and sfx; crowd; wire them into the bus events | `audio.test` passes; listen pass in the browser |\n| **M9 Local multiplayer** | versus setup, select, stage select, results, P2 keyboard/pad maps, local Kachinuki | `versus.test` passes |\n| **M10 Online** | EC4; `KC.Net` with all roles; the card; puppets; prediction; fairness delay; Kachinuki; leave, time-up, end | `online.test` (fake hub) passes, then **the real harness passes** (2p; 4p with latency 150, jitter 50, loss 5; host-leave; server) |\n| **M11 Attract, touch gate and dev** | `KC.Attract`, the touch-only gate, the full dev panel and warps | `attract.test`, `dev.test`, `ui.test` pass |\n| **M12 Polish and ship** | juice and balance passes (Autopilot win-rate table), comfort, a final look review, About text plus `exit-interview.json`, the bundle, **a full manual playthrough**, a no-TODO scan | the full `node tests/run.mjs` prints `0 failed`; the bundle opens from `file://` with no errors; `grep -nE \"TODO|FIXME|XXX|placeholder\"` over `src/` finds nothing |\n\n---\n\n## 17. Riskiest parts and how to de-risk them\n\n| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risking (when) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Karate animations** (spins, back kicks, somersaults, blocks) | `E.MOVES` has no karate-specific techniques; rig spins and airborne flips are unproven | Build the **Technique Lab in M1**, before any content. Prototype the Back Kick and the Front Somersault first. Spin by animating the 3D rig's facing angle. Fallbacks, in order: joint post-processing around the hips (Emberdeep), then a cut mocap clip. Review filmstrips for every technique |\n| **Fair, readable hit detection** | Joint-derived boxes make outcomes depend on animation tuning | The explicit height rules (§4.3) on top of joint boxes; the Lab's **measured gap** vs the table (±4 u, asserted); dev box overlays; quality computed from data, not pixels |\n| **Twin-stick on keyboard feels awkward** | Two-hand chords and keyboard rollover | The WASD + IJKL layout; the 4-frame posture upgrade window; the 0.15 s buffer; face buttons as an alternative; drills that teach it; input display. Test with real keyboards in M1–M3 |\n| **Netplay feel under latency** | Host authority, the 20 msg/s cap, 150 ms latency in the hub test | Deliberate, slow techniques (the source's pace) forgive latency. Add the fairness delay and guest wind-up prediction. **Build the fake hub with latency, jitter and loss at the start of M10** and measure input-to-response time (target ≤ 250 ms at 150 ms one-way). Fallback: a uniform input delay for both sides |\n| **AI quality and exploits** | The source's CPU was exploitable (a TAS found fixed reactions) | Seeded CPU-vs-CPU and Autopilot balance tables in `ai.test`; habit trackers at L8+; mistakes and reaction curves; live dev sliders |\n| **Scope** | 9 matches, 11 locations, 3 bonus games, 3 lessons, story, versus, Kachinuki, online, attract, dev, voices | Data-driven content (§15.3). One `Bout` and one `Karateka` power every mode (story, versus, Kachinuki, online, attract, drills). A vertical slice is playable at M3 |\n| **Hub harness conformance** | The card answers, server mode, time-up grace, traffic both ways, host-leave void | Follow `examples/arena.html`'s structure. Run the real harness headless with Playwright in the test command (§18.3) as soon as M10 starts, with a stub world |\n| **The engine's pause and hit-stop stop `update`** | That stalls networking and makes slow motion change send rates | EC4 live pause; the Bout's own hit-stop; real-time network cadence |\n| **Single-file bundling** | Inline scripts can contain `</script`; the session client must stay unmodified | The build escapes `</script` and a test compares the session client's bytes; the test loads the bundle from `file://` and checks errors |\n| **Environment** | `/tmp` here is a nearly full shared tmpfs (a clone failed with \"No space left on device\"); ports and processes are shared | Keep downloads and caches inside the dev folder; never clone ai-hub; serve with `python3 -m http.server 0 --bind 127.0.0.1` from `vendor/aihub` + the bundle, parse the printed port, fetch the game URL and check for `<title>Karate Champon` before trusting a result, and kill only that PID |\n\n---\n\n## 18. Testing plan\n\n### 18.1 The one command\n`node tests/run.mjs` (from the dev folder) builds first, then runs every suite. It **prints only failing checks** (name and detail) and one final line:\n`KC TESTS: 412 passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (38.2 s)`","numLines":160,"startLine":843,"totalLines":1250}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013UFfZtxwaqJN9Z6vfbqMyb","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
